AU  - N. Tyagi
AU  - T. Gupta
AU  - N. Chhabra
T2  - 2025 3rd International Conference on Communication, Security, and Artificial Intelligence (ICCSAI)
AB  - In this day and age, no matter what age or gender or country the people globally use smartphones and gadgets in their daily lives. Many a times life over social media amuses us with creative content and also connects with virtual society seems to be all the time available to us. The people, agencies, and platforms responsible for sharing verified and positive content are defeated by over inflated count of fake which might have surfaced due to incompetent or slow response from authorities and people looking to take political or financial mileage from these. A fake news might have been shared with the mere purpose of joke or pleasure but could have resulted in panic among people resulting in loss of lives, impact on mental health and financial security. Our objective here is to define fake news and its consequences over social media. We start with basic definition of fake news and its various sources. Further, discussed various intents and contents of spreading fake news over social media. It is followed up with few cases/incidents where positive and negative impacts are realized. At the end concludes with an understanding on overall impact of the fake news over social media, including gaps and the countermeasures.
