TI  - A Teacher-Student Model for Multimodal Fake News Detection
AU  - Y. Ma
AU  - L. Vaiani
AU  - L. Cagliero
T2  - 2025 IEEE 19th International Conference on Application of Information and Communication Technologies (AICT)
AB  - The massive spread of fake news on social media platforms has brought their influence on public opinion and social habits into the spotlight. Today, fake contents appear in both visual and textual sources, thus their early detection and filtering requires the adoption of multimodal learning systems. Multimodal fake news detection involving processing text-image news sources. The main challenge is that features that can be used to effectively discriminate real from fake contents, such as creators’ emotions and intents, are conveyed by a mix of modalities and their extraction requires highly specialized models. In this paper, we explore the use of knowledge distillation to address multimodal fake news detection in text-image news sources. Specifically, we propose a teacher-student model in which student models encoding modality-specific contents distill knowledge from multimodal teachers to accurately detect emotions and intents. The experiments run on the Fakeddit and TI-CNN benchmark datasets evaluate the performance of the fake news classifier based on knowledge distillation, demonstrating its superior performance compared to various baselines.
