TI  - Emotion-Aware Cross Lingual Vision Fake News Detection Using Affective Computing
AU  - A. V
AU  - G. S
AU  - D. J. MJ
T2  - 2026 5th International Conference on Communication, Computing and Electronics Systems (ICCCES)
AB  - The fast spread of emotionally-driven misinformation on social media poses a risk to misleading people and digital health. This paper introduces Emotion-Aware CrossLingualVision (ECLV), which is a model combining affective computing and cross-lingual vision-language analysis to detect fake news. It uses textual embeddings that are multilingual and textual clues of rich language that reflects emotions and CNN-based visual feature of emotion used to capture literal meaning as well as emotions intent of misleading information. Through the derivation of sentiment scores, affective signals and facial expressionbased visual emotions, ECLV creates rich emotionoriented multimodal representations. The joint embeddings are sent through an affectadaptive classifier to separate emotionally influencing fake news content, and that of credible material. Experiments on multilingual data show that the affective features significantly enhance the accuracy of detection of the traditional multimodal models. The findings are clear indications of the capability of ECLV in discovering emotionally misleading tales, crosslinguistic dissonance, and inappropriate sentiments relative to images, which are typically off-radar.
