AB  - This research examines of Deep fake crime, which has become one of the most dangerous and threatening crimes emerging in the digital world as a result of employing advanced Artificial Intelligence algorithms. This study elucidates the serious damages and destruction that have led to the loss of trust in everything that can be heard or seen due to the treacherous manipulation of clips, audio recordings, videos, and images. Therefore, this took a negative toll on societal, economic, political, security, and international levels, given that it infringes upon fundamental human rights that are protected by constitutional and international laws. Furthermore, this study reviews the position of comparative legislation on these newly emerging crimes and examines the adequacy of such legislation in confronting this type of crime. It was found that the existing legislation is insufficient to address this type of crime due to its novelty. As a result, it is necessary to enact strict legislation or introduce amendments to existing legislation with specific provisions criminalizing the use of deep fakes for illegal activities, while imposing deterrent penalties on violators
