TI  - Scalable and Interpretable Engineering Solutions for Fake Account Detection using GNNs and FactorVAE
AU  - L. Selvam
AU  - R. S
AU  - S. Balamurugan
AU  - J. R. Francis Raj
AU  - A. Vegi Fernando
AU  - S. P. Lavanya
T2  - 2026 International Conference on AI-Driven Smart Systems and Ubiquitous Computing (ICAUC)
AB  - The proliferation of social media has introduced complex cybersecurity challenges, particularly due to the widespread presence of fake accounts that manipulate information flow, compromise network integrity, and undermine user trust. Detecting such accounts requires scalable and intelligent engineering solutions capable of analyzing multi-modal data at large scale. This paper presents a hybrid deep learning framework for fake account detection, integrating textual analysis, disentangled representation learning, and graph-based network modeling. Textual content is encoded using RoBERTa embeddings to capture semantic and stylistic features, while FactorVAE disentangles latent factors representing content, style, and intent. Network interactions are modeled through Graph Attention Networks (GAT), capturing relational and structural patterns within social networks. A hybrid MLP-GNN classifier fuses textual and network embeddings to enable high-accuracy detection across large-scale datasets. The framework incorporates explainable AI techniques, including SHAP values and attention maps, to provide interpretable predictions and enhance system reliability. Experimental evaluation demonstrates improved detection accuracy, robustness to adversarial and synthetic accounts, and generalization across multiple social media platforms. By enabling reliable identification of malicious accounts, this approach strengthens cybersecurity measures and ensures safer access to the internet. The proposed system establishes a scalable, interpretable, and efficient engineering solution for fake account detection, providing a benchmark framework for securing social media networks and protecting user interactions in online environments.
