AU  - P. Armenteros-Cosme
AU  - S. Mateos-Plaza
AU  - J. Curto-Hernandez
T2  - 2025 7th International Conference on Frontier Technologies of Information and Computer (ICFTIC)
AB  - This article reviews the state of the art in detecting and mitigating digital disinformation. It covers the classic categories of misinformation, disinformation and malinformation, and moves on to the latest advances in deepfake analysis. Emerging strategies are also examined, drawing on forensic techniques, machine learning, deep learning and blockchain. It also introduces TrueStories, an experimental platform that extends the defence against disinformation to works of fiction based on real events. The system combines three approaches: the automatic generation of an ontology validated by experts; the multimodal comparison of narrative content with a knowledge graph to reveal omissions or misleading dramatic licences; and the analysis of creative intent through metrics of style and emotional charge.
