TI  - Evaluating Machine Learning Strategies For The Detection Of Fake Profiles: A Survey
AU  - A. Negi
AU  - B. Sharma
AU  - S. Kumar
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Emerging Technologies and Innovation for Sustainability (EmergIN)
AB  - The swift development of social media has transformed various domains like business, communication and the way public discussions take place globally. But along with the benefits comes the downside as it has led to a rapid growth in deceptive profiles which are used for evil motives like harming an individual or an organization, spreading false information, impersonation etc. This weakens trust and authenticity of an online space and creates risk for both users and digital platforms. In this paper, we review the challenges and solutions associated with false profile detection across social media platforms. It highlights the pivotal role of Machine Learning (ML) in automating and improving the detection technique and systems. The paper examines various ML types and discusses various ML algorithm and their application under this domain. Beyond this, the paper also talks about various forms of fake account while exploring their intent and the outcomes they produce. It also focuses on ethical and legal implications of fake profiles. The paper further talks about key application areas and outlines various future research directions such as real-time detection and cross-platform analysis.
