TI  - FakeBuster: Multilingual LLM-Based System for Real-Time Automated Verification of News Claims
AU  - S. Toorpu
AU  - V. Vusirikapelly
AU  - S. Nathi
AU  - N. S. S. S. G. Kumar
AU  - M. A. Jabbar
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Intelligent Communication Networks and Computational Techniques (ICICNCT)
AB  - This paper introduces a multilingual, real-time fact check framework that integrates a reasoning engine based on a large language model (LLM) with a dynamic web search mechanism for automated verification of news claims. The proposed system, FakeBuster, is designed to process user-submitted claims and validate their authenticity using live data obtained from the Web. The LLM core is powered by LLaMA-4-Scout-17B-16E-Instruct, and is paired with the Tavily search API to retrieve up-to-date and relevant web content. The framework parses the LLM's outputs to identify function call intents, execute contextual web searches, and return exact verdicts: True, False, Partially True, or Insufficient Information. The system offers multilingual support for the following four languages: English, Hindi, Tamil, and Telugu. The performance of FakeBuster is evaluated using a sample dataset consisting of news from all four languages. The system achieves strong accuracy across languages, with English at $\mathbf{9 8. 0 3 \%}$, Hindi at $\mathbf{9 6. 6 3 \%}$, Tamil at $\mathbf{9 5. 0 9 \%}$, and Telugu at $\mathbf{9 5. 4 \%}$, demonstrating consistent multilingual reliability.
